    "username": "vasuman",
    "nickname": "Vasu",
    "text": "This article articulates the issue with enterprise AI so clearly: the main reason AI pilots fail isn't even because of the AI. \n\nMost enterprises have piloted 3 or more AI projects in the last 12 months. Yet, you won't find any of them on their P&L. Why?\n\n- They built the AI model based on the SOP, but real processes have exceptions that can be 40% of the volume.\n- They thought a quicker W-9 review would improve vendor onboarding. It didn't. That process still takes 22 days.\n- There wasn't a clear owner for the AI agent 7 months in, after the innovation budget ran out and the consultants left.\n\nFantastic article by the former COO of Citadel Securities in the EMEA region. If you've piloted AI projects that never made it to your P&L, read this before piloting another.",
