  {
    "username": "xiaohu",
    "nickname": "小虎",
    "text": "Subvocal：无需出声，也能输入文字的AI眼镜\n\n你无需发出声音，只需做出细微发声动作\n眼镜就能通过感知相关肌肉运动，解析你要输出的内容\n\n再由 AI 将信号转换成文字\n团队宣称，输入速度可超过每分钟 200 个英文单词\n\n视频展示的用途包括：\n向 AI 提问、写消息、操作电脑，以及让两名佩戴者进行旁人听不到的交流",
    "quoted_tweet": {
      "author": "Aarush Yadav",
      "username": "AarushYadav47",
      "text": "We’ve raised $1.3M from YC & Afore Capital so you never have to type or speak again.\n\nTyping is slow. Talking into your computer is awkward. Subvocal fixes both\n\nOur glasses give you the speed of speech without you making a sound or touching a keyboard.\n\nIt tracks your internal speech muscles with non-contact sensing and decodes silent, almost invisible mouthing into text at more than 200 words/min.\n\nPre-orders are now live at:\nhttp://subvocal.co/preorder?utm_source=x"
    },
    "url": "https://x.com/xiaohu/status/2116445350865367066",
    "time": "2026-10-31 16:21",
    "created_at": "Sat Oct 31 08:21:07 +0000 2026",
    "id_str": "2116445350865367066",
    "is_retweet": false
  },
  {
    "username": "xiaohu",
    "nickname": "小虎",
    "text": "陶哲轩：AI 时代要主动锻炼思考能力\n\n陶哲轩用粮食生产作类比：\n\n生产革命让食物便宜、充足\n人们却开始需要主动控制饮食、安排运动。\n\n过去，体力劳动自然提供了锻炼；今天，这件事需要刻意维护。\n\n同理：AI 让脑力任务变得便宜、容易，但生活中原本自带的思考训练会随之减少...\n\n因此，人们需要注意自己的“精神食粮”，主动保持解决问题的能力，锻炼你的大脑...\n\n否则，有些人可能越来越依赖 AI，一旦失去工具，就难以应对现实问题...",
    "quoted_tweet": {
      "author": "Dany",
      "username": "danysvnt",
      "text": "TERENCE TAO SAYS AI WILL DO TO OUR BRAINS WHAT CHEAP FOOD DID TO OUR BODIES\n\nfor most of history life was the workout. then food got cheap and people had to start watching their diet on purpose\n\ntao says thinking is next:\n\"you have to watch your mental diet, and you do have to maintain mental exercise\"\n\nMIT had students write essays with ChatGPT. minutes later 83% couldn't quote a single sentence they'd \"written\"\n\nthe ones who wrote on their own first and got ChatGPT later used it better, and their brain activity went up\n\nthe struggle before the answer is the part your brain keeps\n\nan answer you didn't work for is easy to get and even easier to forget\n\nwould you let your kid use AI for homework from day one, or make them struggle first?"
    },
    "url": "https://x.com/xiaohu/status/2116448508593283300",
